  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =cos\\,(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =cos\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
